/Baisan\">Baisan</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baindari\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Baindari\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107366973\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107366973\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3633240</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Baindari</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">George A. Kennedy</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"15\" data-page-number=\"15\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/27\" data-page-index=\"27\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/27\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;27\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>BAINDARI</b> \u62dc\u97f3\u9054\u91cc d. 1607, bore the clan-name Nara and was <i>beile</i> of the Hoifa tribe which formed part of the H\u016blun nation. (For the other three tribes, Hada, Yehe, and Ula, see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wan\">Wan</a></span>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Yangginu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Yangginu\">Yangginu</a></span> and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Bujantai\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Bujantai\">Bujantai</a></span> respectively.) Baindari's ancestors possessed the family name Ikderi and belonged originally to the Nimaca tribe on the banks of the Amur river. Migrating southward to Jaru they put themselves under the protection of some Nara clansmen. Then, after slaying seven oxen in a sacrifice to Heaven, they exchanged their own name for that of their protectors. Six generations later one of their descendants, Wangginu, consolidated his position by establishing a city at Mt. H\u00fbrki on the Hoifa river, where the natural advantages of his location enabled him to withstand repeated attacks from the Mongols. On the death of Wangginu his grandson, Baindari, murdered the seven uncles who might have stood in his way and proclaimed himself <i>beile</i> of the Hoifa. In 1593 he joined the confederation against <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Nurhaci\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Nurhaci\">Nurhaci</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] which was unsuccessfully led by <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Narimbulu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Narimbulu\">Narimbulu</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] of the Yehe tribe. Two years later Nurhaci retaliated by taking the town of Dobi from Baindari and killing two of his generals. In 1597 the H\u00fblun tribes agreed on a truce with the enemy and thereafter Baindari, whose territory was situated between the Yehe towns and Nurhaci's center of operations, wavered in allegiance from one to the other, finally deciding to trust in the impregnability of his city to defend him against both. In 1607, however, Nurhaci invaded the region, killed Baindari and his son, and thus put an end to the independent existence of the Hoifa tribe.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/229/13b; Hauer, E., <i>K'ai-kuo fang-l\u00fceh</i>, pp. 29, 35\u201337; <i>Ch'ing T'ai-tsu Wu Huang-ti shih-lu</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Nurhaci\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Nurhaci\">Nurhaci</a></span>) 1/3b]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">George A. Kennedy</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Bahai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Baisan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Bujantai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Narimbulu"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Nurhaci"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Yangginu"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:George A. Kennedy"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = baindari\n | previous = Bahai\n | next     = Baisan\n | from     = 27\n | to       = 27\n | notes    = \n | section_author = George A. Kennedy\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Baindari}}"}}}